{
  "id": "80742",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Entropy and The Second Law of Thermodynamics",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Processes that involve an increase in entropy of the system (Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sys"
              },
              {
                "text": " > 0) are very often spontaneous. However, examples of nonspontaneous processes are plentiful. By considering entropy changes to include changes in the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "surroundings"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "All matter other than the system being studied."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3649188051",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "585548317",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " (Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": "), we see that the relationship between surroundings and spontaneity is significant. In thermodynamic models, the system and surroundings comprise everything—that is, the universe—so the following is true: "
              }
            ],
            "id": "u56c4795eo86gyg",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "8iouy63clunb3o1",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "u90797gtx59le1y",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{surr}}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "This expanded view of Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "text": " brings us to the second law of thermodynamics. "
              }
            ],
            "id": "le2yqmbhddnrixh",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "2ki8e12qxdx47g1",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "qk0ny8sqbduvcdu",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "m4kh98xmb6aareb",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "sz3f0058kyppxsi",
            "items": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2093297032",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "All spontaneous changes cause an increase in the entropy of the universe."
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "10839473",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{surr}}\\;>\\;0",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3369161312",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Δ"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "S"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "univ"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " is positive"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Process is spontaneous"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "tr"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Δ"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "S"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "univ"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " is negative"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Process is not spontaneous"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "tr"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Δ"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "S"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "univ"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " is zero"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "Process is at equilibrium"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "td"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "tr"
                      }
                    ],
                    "rowstyle": "alternating",
                    "type": "table"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3898233341",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "dd"
              }
            ],
            "title": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " The Second Law of Thermodynamics "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3701844727",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "type": "dl"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "zw3knewyve9ca0l",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "umwlmghxre6hftb",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Let's examine the factors that contribute to the change in entropy of a system and its surroundings. For example, consider the combustion of one mole of methane, where the methane and oxygen reaction is the system. In this exothermic process, 241.8 kJ of heat is transferred from the system to the surroundings. The heat added to the surroundings causes the kinetic energy of the particles of the surroundings to increase, thereby increasing the entropy of the surroundings. However, heat transfer is not the only factor that affects Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": ". The temperature of the surroundings also impacts its entropy change. The combustion of one mole of methane adds 241.8 kJ to the surroundings, regardless of their temperature. However, the particles in higher-temperature surroundings are moving much more rapidly than the particles in lower-temperature surroundings, so the addition of that amount of energy has less of an impact on the entropy of the the higher-temperature surroundings. Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": " increases with increasing amounts of heat transferred to the surroundings and decreases with increasing temperature of the surroundings. The relationship is:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vk9v62m4bo83n29",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "4moo49b13tidwgq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "8tf5c2d6dinb1fa",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{surr}}\\;=\\;\\frac{q_{\\mathrm{rev}}}T",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "where "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "q"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "rev"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the heat absorbed from or given to the surroundings in a reversible process, and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "T"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the temperature in kelvins."
              }
            ],
            "id": "urtw4adoxc48r0x",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "463193886",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "activity_id": 78668,
            "id": "3899970212",
            "type": "activity-reference"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3332372628",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "didigetthis",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For many realistic applications, the surroundings are vast in comparison to the system. In such cases, the heat gained or lost by the surroundings as a result of some process represents a very small—nearly infinitesimal—fraction of its total thermal energy. For example, combustion of a fuel in air involves transfer of heat from a system (the fuel and oxygen molecules undergoing reaction) to surroundings that are essentially infinitely more massive (the earth’s atmosphere). As a result, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "q"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": " is a good approximation of "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "q"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "rev"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and the second law may be stated as the following:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "dmjjx0z25rtdfrs",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "psr37vh9liroqyu",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "mdbcfno9xbxh9h3",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{surr}}\\; =\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\frac{q_{\\mathrm{surr}}}T\\;>\\;0",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Note that if the pressure is constant (which is usually the case), "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "q"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": " = Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "surr"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "la4pam26u57r2to",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2137834693",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consider the melting of ice and the associated thermodynamic properties for this process: "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "gcxjfs3w8ak4vk4",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "fgp4cdodzm9zu9c",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "w58u3vwbxswaus7",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(s)\\;\\longrightarrow\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{with}\\;\\; \\mathrm\\Delta H^\\circ\\;=\\;6.01\\;\\mathrm{kJ}\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm\\Delta S^\\circ\\; =\\;22.0\\;\\frac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This means that when 1 mole of ice is melted, the entropy of the system increases by 22.0 J/K and 6.01 kJ of heat are transferred from the surroundings to the system. For our calculations, we assume that these values do not change with temperature. (This is an approximation, but it is sufficiently accurate for our purposes.)"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "pl5ety7ulr8ffuh",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Is this process spontaneous at −10.0 °C? Is it spontaneous at +10.0 °C? At what temperature will the solid and liquid phases be at equilibrium?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "htqf2waqm7sgfc2",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "At −10.0 °C"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3iyy9pm5yiqysiw",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " We can assess the spontaneity of the process by calculating the entropy change of the universe. The entropy change of the system, Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sys"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is 22.0 J/K. The enthalpy change of the system, Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sys"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is 6.01 kJ, so the enthalpy change of the surroundings, Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "surr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is −6.01 kJ. Substituting these values and the temperature in kelvins into the second law equation gives:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "730ecn1rd28y8kx",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "lxqk4y108fulpqm",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "80m07lok4wflofp",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{c}\\mathrm\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;\\mathrm\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm\\Delta H_{\\mathrm{surr}}}T\\\\=\\;22.0\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\;+\\;\\dfrac{-6.01\\times10^3\\;\\mathrm J}{263.2\\;\\mathrm K}\\;\\;\\\\=\\;22.0\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\;-\\;22.8\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\\\\\;=\\;-0.8\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "univ"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is less than 0, so ice melting at −10.0 °C is nonspontaneous (not spontaneous)."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wcsqmujvc0qyt07",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "At 10.0 °C"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "o0rjijawkwbtrc6",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Except for temperature, all the values are the same as for the previous calculation. Substituting into the second law equation gives:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "r4h16o5ockujw3t",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "7t96imcyej1agub",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cpzu6d4qsnk4ome",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{c}\\mathrm\\Delta{\\mathrm S}_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;{\\mathrm{ΔS}}_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\;+\\;\\dfrac{{\\mathrm{ΔH}}_{\\mathrm{surr}}}{\\mathrm T}\\\\=\\;22.0\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\;+\\;\\dfrac{-6.01\\times10^3\\;\\mathrm J}{283.2\\;\\mathrm K}\\;\\;\\\\=\\;22.0\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\;-\\;21.2\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\\\\\;=\\;0.8\\;\\dfrac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "univ"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is greater than 0, so ice melting at 10.0 °C is spontaneous."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "zztds6bvjqvetdf",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "Solid and Liquid in Equilibrium"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u05jisbe17npuyb",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "When a system is at equilibrium, Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "univ"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 0. We use the same equation as for the previous calculations, but we set Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "univ"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " equal to 0:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vq6mf0j97fc9ilm",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "2g66lq95yd49kb3",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "fvwpl8x468xezvc",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;=\\;\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{univ}}\\;+\\;\\frac{\\Delta H_{\\mathrm{surr}}}T\\; =\\;22.0\\;\\frac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\;+\\;\\frac{-6,010\\;\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm T}\\;=\\;0",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Solving for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "T"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", we find:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vdyxt82car92spb",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "0u6bzhkj9qogzhh",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "05n0v39m13hb8bn",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "T\\;=\\;\\frac{6,010\\;\\mathrm J}{\\;22.0\\;\\;\\mathrm J/\\mathrm K}\\;=\\;273\\;\\mathrm K",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Solid and liquid in H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O are in equilibrium at 373 K, or 0 °C. The solid and liquid phases of a substance are in equilibrium at the substance's freezing (melting) point."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bakar61xg2t79km",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1570464370",
